---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend";
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS to Omnisend: Shopify migration decisions";
const desc = "Assess the Omnisend migration route after Yotpo messaging retirement, with destination-specific acceptance checks.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I keep sending through Yotpo during this migration?",
    "answer": "Do not plan on it. The messaging login reports decommissioned dashboard and background services. Confirm available records with support; do not promise a retired-sender rollback."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is the key Omnisend acceptance decision?",
    "answer": "Verify file-based channel status and rebuilt workflow enrollment before activating the combined journeys."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do Reviews and Loyalty move with messaging?",
    "answer": "Treat them as separate services and data dependencies. Name the owner of review requests and points messages, and verify any required destination integration."
  },
  {
    "question": "Were the migration checks on this page performed?",
    "answer": "No. They are proposed checks for a receiving account. Production delivery, permissions, recovery and account-specific costs require separate validation."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <nav><a class="link" href="/apps">Tool catalog</a> · <a class="link" href="/guides/selection-framework">Selection framework</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS is a migration question now. Its messaging login reports that the application and background services are decommissioned. Reviews and Loyalty are separate decisions. An old export or implementation guide does not prove that a retired dashboard can still be opened. For Omnisend, the central task is rebuilding channel permissions and automation enrollment from saved data, rather than choosing which live Yotpo suite to renew.</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Start with the files you actually possess</h2>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/12048785-migrate-from-yotpo-to-omnisend">current Omnisend migration guide</a> says automated Yotpo contact sync is no longer available. It describes file import and manual workflow rebuilding. Treat its old Yotpo export steps as historical if your account is inaccessible; ask support about available records before planning a recovery date.</p>
      <p>Create a manifest for each saved file: store, export date, channel, consent source and suppression coverage. A phone field is not SMS permission. Separate contacts with documented email permission, documented SMS permission, both, and neither. Keep uncertain records out of promotional enrollment while their status is resolved.</p>
      <h2>Prevent import from behaving like a new signup</h2>
      <p>Proposed acceptance case: import staff-controlled records representing email-only, SMS-only, both-channel and unsubscribed customers into an isolated destination setup. Inspect each channel status and every welcome queue before enabling delivery. An existing customer imported for continuity should not automatically receive an acquisition discount.</p>
      <p>Check mapping updates against an existing unsubscribed destination contact as well as a new contact. Record whether the import overwrites properties or status, and reconcile accepted and rejected rows. A matching total cannot show that the right people remained suppressed.</p>
      <h2>Rebuild journeys by eligibility, not by copied delays</h2>
      <p>Inventory the saved welcome, cart and post-purchase definitions. For each, write the original entry event, exclusions, exit event and intended recipient. Recreate these rules before recreating message styling. Use current Shopify orders to exclude completed purchases from cart recovery; historical imports should not restart purchase-triggered messages.</p>
      <p>Proposed mixed-channel check: a customer buys after entering cart recovery and unsubscribes from SMS while still subscribed to email. Inspect all remaining steps. Purchase completion should remove obsolete recovery, and channel changes should affect the relevant channel without granting permission elsewhere. Do not carry over a universal cross-channel delay from an old template.</p>
      <h2>Treat the sending number as a separate workstream</h2>
      <p>Omnisend documents a transfer route for an existing verified toll-free number. Confirm ownership, eligibility and the actual port status with support before updating forms. Do not promise a transfer deadline from this page. Preserve opt-in disclosures and identify the sender customers will recognize.</p>
      <p>Email domain authentication, SMS readiness and browser push permission are separate acceptance items. Do not interpret an imported email address as a push subscriber. Enable only the channels whose permission and destination setup have been checked.</p>
      <h2>Release checklist, costs and evidence limits</h2>
      <p>Keep destination sends paused until eligible counts, suppressions, capture routes and representative queues reconcile. Name one owner for every automated message across Shopify, retained Yotpo modules and the receiving stack. If a destination check fails, pause that destination queue and repair it; the retired Yotpo sender is not a rollback option.</p>
      <p>Compare the receiving subscription, messaging usage, implementation work and retained Reviews or Loyalty costs. Sequenzy or another email service belongs in that budget only if its required integration and operating role are demonstrated. There is no evidenced universal winner or fixed price here.</p>
      <p>Checked against primary supplier material on 24 November 2026 and the <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo decommission notice</a>. These are proposed acceptance cases, not performed merchant tests. Historical data recovery, legal sufficiency, account entitlements and production delivery remain unverified. Related migration assessments: <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend">Omnisend</a>, <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-postscript">Postscript</a>, <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-privy">Privy</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
